    {
      "id": "2sq6fcn",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Mahatma Gandhi (1869–1948)"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Mahatma Gandhi (1869–1948) spearheaded the non-violent freedom struggle in India.",
        "Subhas Chandra Bose (1897–1945) established leadership in the Indian National Army (Azad Hind Fauj).",
        "Bhagat Singh (1907–1931) remains a prominent symbol of revolutionary nationalism.",
        "The 'Lal-Bal-Pal' nationalist trio consisted of Lala Lajpat Rai (1865–1928), Bal Gangadhar Tilak (1856–1920), and Bipin Chandra Pal (1858–1932).",
        "Sardar Vallabhbhai Patel (1875–1950) and Jawaharlal Nehru (1889–1964) were pivotal figures in nation-building and Indian administration."
      ],
      "id": "4329o8c"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "3a4g7ot",
      "content": "• Known as the 'Father of the Nation'."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "hmjjfa1",
      "content": "• Leader of the Indian National Movement."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "5ir2kxz",
      "content": "• Introduced Satyagraha and non-violent resistance."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "8woe80n",
      "content": "• Led Non-Cooperation (1920), Civil Disobedience (1930), Quit India (1942)."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "nw83jye",
      "content": "• Led the Dandi March in 1930."
    },
    {
      "id": "9bv9445",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Subhas Chandra Bose (1897–1945)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "hibegx2",
      "content": "• Popularly known as Netaji."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "bvca51i",
      "content": "• Founded the Indian National Army (INA)."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "sm04yow",
      "content": "• Gave the slogan 'Give me blood and I will give you freedom'."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "pvcvto6",
      "content": "• Formed the Azad Hind Government."
    },
    {
      "id": "f233sui",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Bhagat Singh (1907–1931)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "on9l169",
      "content": "• Famous revolutionary freedom fighter."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "8p7lmhf",
      "content": "• Involved in the Lahore Conspiracy Case."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "7nnd1we",
      "content": "• Along with Batukeshwar Dutt threw bombs in the Central Legislative Assembly in 1929."
    },
    {
      "type": "pullQuote",
      "content": "Chapter 14: Freedom Fighters of India",
      "id": "zwm972r"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "dfeovlc",
      "content": "• Executed by the British in 1931."
    },
    {
      "id": "a3m3xwi",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Rani Lakshmibai (1828–1858)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "7limn7j",
      "content": "• Queen of Jhansi and leader in the Revolt of 1857."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "a6dozro",
      "content": "• Fought bravely against British forces."
    },
    {
      "id": "nhkpkkb",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Bal Gangadhar Tilak (1856–1920)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "81uynwi",
      "content": "• Known as the 'Father of Indian Unrest'."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "2j2j15s",
      "content": "• Gave slogan 'Swaraj is my birthright and I shall have it'."
    },
    {
      "id": "51w635v",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Lala Lajpat Rai (1865–1928)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "u3yaf7a",
      "content": "• Known as 'Punjab Kesari'."
    },
